+The controls support this explanation without proving it for other tasks. Literal wording improved matched accuracy by \literalControlChange{} points, with \literalControlWins{} wins and no losses. Across all outputs, distractor capture was \distractorCaptureRate{}\%, exact-output compliance was \exactOutputComplianceRate{}\%, and invalid output was \invalidOutputRate{}\%. The failures therefore arose mainly from selecting the competing code, not from ignoring the requested format.
