-\section{Reproducibility Statement}
-% TODO(agent): exact model filename + checksum; raw probe manifest; make all
-% regenerates scored results from cached outputs; make clean-deep && make all
-% repeats inference; gates enforce frozen inputs, citations, and number provenance.
+The findings concern one small quantized model and may not transfer to larger models or other quantization levels. Synthetic clause lookup is not natural contract analysis, and retrieval accuracy is not a measure of general capability. The \cpuBudgetMinutes{}-minute CPU budget capped the grid, leaving only \tierEightCount{} full-context probes at the longest tier and wide intervals throughout. Greedy decoding removes run-to-run sampling variation but does not show how sampling would change the estimates. The mitigation is a deliberately simple keyword filter rather than a learned retrieval system. Finally, the experiment varies prompts only up to \tierEightTokens{} mean tokens, so it cannot rule out degradation beyond the measured range.
+
+\section{Reproducibility}
+
+Every reported quantity is generated by analysis scripts from the committed probe manifest and raw model outputs, following the reporting principle that computational evidence should expose its budget and variation \citep{dodge2019show}. The model and cached data are frozen and checksummed, and each raw output retains its stable probe identifier. Running \texttt{make all} regenerates \texttt{results.json}, the LaTeX value macros, and the paper from cached outputs; running \texttt{make clean-deep \&\& make all} repeats deterministic model inference. Repository gates check frozen inputs, citation resolution, number provenance, pipeline freshness, result sanity, prose style, anonymity, and compilation.
 
